@@ -99,6 +99,15 @@ DU output is written into the FIFO before TC can consume it on the following
 edge. There is no payload bypass. The FIFO head is combinational, without an
 additional output register.
 
+The current main implementation also registers a redundant one-hot decode of
+the nonempty head. It advances from `d.head`/`d.count` on the same accepted
+edge as the original Bridge state, resets to zero, and holds on rejected edges.
+The combinational payload read ORs the selected FIFO slot. This preserves the
+old head visibility, empty value, metadata blocking, credit accounting and
+non-bypass latency. The original 19,147-record regression checks the resulting
+head data as well as every logical state bit. Physical results are recorded in
+the [10 ns experiment](../experiments/msu_fmax/target_10ns_20261110/README.md).
+
 When the head has `k=0` and result metadata is full, `head_valid=0`. Metadata is
 pushed when TC accepts the tile's first packet and popped on the **actual
 TC→MSU handshake**, without waiting for HBM writeback completion.
